{
  "note": "The game menu and its settings (docs/specs/domains/MENU.md UI-005 to UI-010; F-UI-MENU 1, F-UI-SETTINGS 1). Settings belong to the device, not the save: the slice keeps them in the browser apart from the save. Each setting: a type (switch, choice, range), its default and, for a range, min, max and step. Controls are per platform (UI-010): keyboard and mouse, gamepad, touch; each action is bound once per context, and 'anywhere' actions may not share a control with any context. The slice is played on keyboard and mouse; the gamepad and touch mappings are the defaults for when those platforms come (UI-004, PH3). The menu's look is Painted signs (ADR-0033, UI-015, UI-016): its home screen shows every tab as a painted board, in the order given here; each tab has a group (You, Town, Game), a colour from menu.colours (board colour, lettering colour; the accents of ART_DIRECTION 2.3 as they look in shade) and may be a tall or a small board; small boards of the Game group are painted in the quiet colour. Checked by world.settings_problems().",
